To add an interactive tooltip to an SVG, the cleanest approach is to wrap the SVG in a container element (`div`) and use CSS for the tooltip styling. This keeps your SVG code clean and allows you to use standard web accessibility patterns.

### 1. The HTML/SVG Structure
Wrap your SVG in a `div` with a class of `tooltip-container`. We will add a `span` inside that container to act as the tooltip text.

```html
<div class="tooltip-container">
  <!-- Your SVG goes here -->
  <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 32 32" ...>
    <!-- ... rest of your SVG code ... -->
  </svg>

  <!-- The tooltip text -->
  <span class="tooltip-text">This is my tooltip!</span>
</div>
```

### 2. The CSS
We use `position: relative` on the container and `position: absolute` on the tooltip so it can float above the SVG.

```css
.tooltip-container {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-block;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.tooltip-text {
  visibility: hidden;
  width: 120px;
  background-color: #333;
  color: #fff;
  text-align: center;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 5px 0;

  /* Position the tooltip */
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 1;
  bottom: 125%; /* Position above the icon */
  left: 50%;
  margin-left: -60px; /* Center the tooltip */

  /* Fade-in effect */
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity 0.3s;
}

/* Show the tooltip when hovering over the container */
.tooltip-container:hover .tooltip-text {
  visibility: visible;
  opacity: 1;
}
```

### Why this is the best method:
1. **Accessibility:** By keeping the tooltip in the DOM, you can easily add `aria-label` attributes to the SVG container so screen readers understand what the icon represents.
2. **Performance:** You aren't manipulating the DOM with heavy JavaScript libraries; CSS handles the rendering, which is highly performant.
3. **Maintainability:** If you want to change the text or the styling of the tooltip, you don't have to touch the complex SVG path data or filter definitions.

### Pro-Tip: Adding an Arrow
If you want a small "pointer" arrow on the bottom of the tooltip, add this to your CSS:

```css
.tooltip-text::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: 100%; /* At the bottom of the tooltip */
  left: 50%;
  margin-left: -5px;
  border-width: 5px;
  border-style: solid;
  border-color: #333 transparent transparent transparent;
}
```

### Important note on your SVG:
Since your SVG uses `filter="url(#filter0_...)"`, ensure that the `id` values inside your `<defs>` tag remain unique if you plan on having multiple icons on the same page. If you duplicate the SVG, the IDs might conflict and break the shadows!

